      "worked": "The bearing differences give $\\angle AOB=220^\\circ-100^\\circ=120^\\circ$, $\\angle BOC=310^\\circ-220^\\circ=90^\\circ$ and $\\angle COA=360^\\circ-310^\\circ+100^\\circ=150^\\circ$.\nSince $O$ is inside $\\triangle ABC$, add the areas of $\\triangle AOB$, $\\triangle BOC$ and $\\triangle COA$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Area}&=\\frac12(25)(40)\\sin120^\\circ+\\frac12(40)(50)\\sin90^\\circ+\\frac12(50)(25)\\sin150^\\circ\\\\\n\\text{Area}&=250\\sqrt3+1000+\\frac{625}{2}\\text{ m}^2\\\\\n\\text{Area}&\\approx1745.5\\text{ m}^2.\n\\end{align*}$$",
